--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@ package, not for somebody reading this repository's commit log.
 
 ### Fixed
 
+- **`afterModelResponse` now receives the usage of every provider call in the turn, not just the last.** A turn that ran tools makes one provider call per round, and the hook was handed only the final call's `usage`, so a deployer billing or budgeting from it under-counted exactly the expensive turns. `inputTokens`, `outputTokens` and `totalTokens` are now each summed over the calls that reported usage; a call whose provider reported none adds nothing, and a turn in which no call reported usage still passes `undefined`. The hook's third parameter is now typed `TurnUsage` (exported from the package entry point, structurally identical to `UsageMetadata`), so the signature says it is a turn total. **Migration note**: a turn that called no tools reports exactly what it did before, but for a tool-calling turn the numbers your hook records will grow — that is the correction, so recheck any budget threshold tuned against the old figures.
 - `onError` and `afterSession` hooks now fire when `beforeSession` throws, matching the guarantee the hook names imply. Previously, a throw from `beforeSession` escaped the `try`/`finally` block entirely, so neither hook ran. **Migration note**: if your `afterSession` hook assumed it would only be called after a full session turn, it will now also be called when `beforeSession` itself fails — the hook can inspect the session to detect this case (no entries beyond the initial user message will have been processed).
 
