-- `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L148](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L148)), and is passed the `lastUsage` local — the most recent round's usage, not a sum across tool rounds, so a deployer using the hook for billing or audit under-counts every turn that ran tools.
+These properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` record the measured semantics that hook features specify against. The `onError` boundary remains out of scope; issue #93 defines the aggregate usage delivered after tool rounds.
+
+- The `catch` gates `onError` on `error instanceof Error` ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L152](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L152)), so a rejection that is not an `Error` — a thrown string or object — bypasses `onError` entirely while still propagating to the caller.
+- `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits and receives the summed provider-call usage for the entire turn, so tool rounds are included in a deployer's billing or audit total ([validated by: reports the summed usage from every provider call in a turn with two tool rounds](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestratorUsage.acceptance.test.ts#L44)).
+- The hook's third parameter is typed `TurnUsage`, exported from the package entry point and documented as the sum over every provider call in the turn, so a consumer learns it is a total from the signature rather than the orchestrator ([validated by: is the public type afterModelResponse receives for a turn](../../src/orchestration/turnUsage.test.ts#L10)).
+- Each token field is summed across the provider calls that reported usage ([validated by: sums each token field of two reported rounds](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L31)).
+- When no earlier provider call in the turn reported usage, the first call that does supplies the running total unchanged ([validated by: adopts the round usage when no earlier round reported any](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L39)).
+- A provider call that reports no usage adds nothing to the running total rather than turning it `undefined` or `NaN` ([validated by: keeps the running total when the round reported nothing](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L43)).
